---
import ProofEquation from './ProofEquation.astro';
import {hxEquations, retainedPressureFE, proofAssets} from '../lib/aero/hx-proof';
---
<section data-hx-walkthrough data-panel="guide" hidden aria-label="Guided heat-exchanger proof notebook">
  <header class="hx-heading"><small>GUIDED FIRST PRINCIPLES · SYNTHETIC CASE</small><h3>One tube. Three load cases. A checked working notebook.</h3><p>Ask questions on the left. Review the controlled inputs and evidence here. A model explanation cannot change these calculations or declare the tube safe.</p></header>
  <div class="hx-scope">Browser-local analytical calculations · retained educational FE comparison · no new conventional solver run.</div>
  <div class="hx-summary" aria-label="Current analytical predictions"><div><small>Pressure-only bore hoop</small><strong data-hx-hoop>21.048 MPa</strong></div><div><small>Thermal-only free extension</small><strong data-hx-extension>1.280 mm</strong></div><div><small>Thermal-only fixed stress</small><strong data-hx-stress>−243.200 MPa</strong></div></div>
  <p class="hx-live-note" data-hx-status role="status" aria-live="polite">Assumed inputs · not yet reviewed.</p>
  <section data-hx-step="0"><span class="hx-number">01 / QUESTION</span><h4>What would pressure and heat do to this tube?</h4><p>Predict stresses in a closed-end pressure tube. Separately compare heating a sliding tube with heating one whose axial ends cannot move. Before inspecting any FEA contour, establish the expected loads, signs and scale.</p>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 600 140" class="hx-diagram" role="img" aria-labelledby="hx-diagram-title"><title id="hx-diagram-title">Idealized straight heat-exchanger tube; schematic, not a computed field</title><rect x="70" y="40" width="455" height="50" rx="4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M70 52H525M70 78H525M95 65H500M488 59L500 65L488 71" stroke="currentColor" fill="none"/><text x="72" y="26" fill="currentColor" font-size="12">Pressure-only: closed ends · uniform wall · away from end effects</text><text x="72" y="119" fill="currentColor" font-size="12">Thermal-only: one end free OR both ends axially fixed</text></svg>
    <div class="hx-callout"><strong>The engineering question stays fixed.</strong><p>Equation consistency and idealized FE verification—not exchanger design release. No real alloy allowable or test correlation has been supplied.</p></div><button type="button" data-hx-ask="Explain the three separate load cases in this synthetic heat-exchanger notebook. Why are closed-end pressure and axial thermal restraint different assumptions? Do not combine them or claim hardware safety.">Ask Aero about this question ↗</button>
  </section>
  <section data-hx-step="1" hidden><span class="hx-number">02 / ASSUMPTIONS</span><h4>Review the physics before the answer.</h4><p>All values are synthetic assumptions. Constant isotropic elasticity; uniform temperature; transverse surfaces traction-free in the thermal cases. Outside gauge pressure stays zero.</p>
    <form data-hx-inputs class="hx-inputs">
      <label>Inside gauge pressure (MPa)<input name="pressure" type="number" min="0" max="10" step="any" value="2" required /></label>
      <label>Bore radius (mm)<input name="radius" type="number" min="1" max="100" step="any" value="10" required /></label>
      <label>Wall thickness (mm)<input name="thickness" type="number" min="0.1" max="20" step="any" value="1" required /></label>
      <label>Length (m)<input name="length" type="number" min="0.05" max="5" step="any" value="1" required /></label>
      <label>Elastic modulus (GPa)<input name="modulus" type="number" min="1" max="500" step="any" value="190" required /></label>
      <label>Poisson ratio ν<input name="poisson" type="number" min="-0.9" max="0.49" step="any" value="0.3" required /></label>
      <label>Expansion coefficient (10⁻⁶/K)<input name="alpha" type="number" min="0" max="50" step="any" value="16" required /></label>
      <label>Temperature change (K)<input name="temperature" type="number" min="-200" max="200" step="any" value="80" required /></label>
      <button type="submit">Apply inputs & recalculate</button><button type="button" data-hx-review>Review these synthetic assumptions</button>
    </form><p class="hx-muted">Apply is explicit. Draft values do not alter the working record until applied. Any applied edit removes the previous assumption review and invalidates mismatched retained FE evidence.</p>
    <button type="button" data-hx-ask="Review the applicability of the controlled inputs and assumptions in this tube notebook. Identify omissions that would matter for a real heat exchanger. Do not invent certified material data or alter inputs.">Ask Aero to challenge the assumptions ↗</button>
  </section>
  <section data-hx-step="2" hidden><span class="hx-number">03 / DERIVATION</span><h4>Derive, then substitute.</h4><p>Compatibility and equilibrium determine the pressure field. Pressure tractions determine A and B. Closed-end thrust sets axial stress. Thermal boundary conditions decide whether expansion or compression results.</p>
    {hxEquations.slice(0,4).map(e=><><ProofEquation label={e.title} latex={e.latex}/><p class="hx-muted">{e.assumptions}</p></>)}
    <div class="hx-substitution" data-hx-substitution></div>
    <button type="button" data-hx-ask="Walk through the Lamé boundary-value derivation and the separate thermal strain relation in this notebook, step by step. Explain the units and sign conventions. Use the supplied deterministic values, not invented ones.">Ask Aero to explain the derivation ↗</button>
  </section>
  <section data-hx-step="3" hidden><span class="hx-number">04 / EQUATION CHECKS</span><h4>Challenge the calculated field.</h4><p>Test both pressure tractions, end-force equilibrium, radial differential equilibrium and the thermal limiting cases. These algebraic checks can expose implementation errors. They do not validate real material or model-form assumptions.</p>
    <div class="hx-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Normalized identity residual</th><th>State</th></tr></thead><tbody data-hx-checks></tbody></table></div>
    <p class="hx-muted">Identity-check tolerance: 10⁻¹⁰, for floating-point consistency only—not a universal engineering acceptance limit. The published Python verification also contains nine executable tests.</p>
    <button type="button" data-hx-ask="Explain why passing these equation-identity checks does not establish physical validation, material suitability, buckling resistance or exchanger safety. Which independent checks are still missing?">Ask Aero what these checks do not prove ↗</button>
  </section>
  <section data-hx-step="4" hidden><span class="hx-number">05 / FE COMPARISON</span><h4>Compare with a different calculation—not with a confident answer.</h4><p>The retained Python calculation assembles and solves a radial FE stiffness matrix plus a constant axial-strain degree of freedom. It is an educational implementation, not ANSYS or CalculiX.</p>
    <ProofEquation label={hxEquations[4].title} latex={hxEquations[4].latex}/>
    <div class="hx-callout" data-hx-fe-state role="status"></div>
    <div data-hx-fe-current><img src={`${proofAssets}/pressure-convergence.svg`} width="680" height="375" alt="Retained pressure FE stress error decreases through 4, 8, 16, 32 and 64 radial elements." loading="lazy"/><div class="hx-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Elements</th><th>Stress L₂ error</th><th>Outer displacement error</th></tr></thead><tbody>{retainedPressureFE.map(row=><tr><td>{row.elements}</td><td>{(row.gauss_stress_relative_L2_error*100).toFixed(4)}%</td><td>{(row.outer_u_relative_error*100).toFixed(6)}%</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p>Separate free/fixed thermal FE cases agree to floating-point precision. They are not combined-load exchanger qualification.</p></div>
    <p class="hx-muted">The retained numerical values only apply to the exact reference inputs. Changed inputs require a new FE calculation; this page does not silently reuse the old PASS.</p>
    <div class="hx-links"><a href={`${proofAssets}/results.json`}>Retained FE record ↗</a><a href={`${proofAssets}/verify.py`}>Reproduction code ↗</a><a href={`${proofAssets}/manifest.json`}>Source hashes ↗</a></div>
  </section>
  <section data-hx-step="5" hidden><span class="hx-number">06 / DISPOSITION</span><h4>A bounded conclusion. An explicit next question.</h4><dl class="hx-disposition"><div><dt>Equation consistency</dt><dd data-hx-equation-state>PASS</dd></div><div><dt>FE comparison for active inputs</dt><dd data-hx-comparison-state>Retained reference only</dd></div><div><dt>Assumption review</dt><dd data-hx-review-state>NOT REVIEWED</dd></div><div><dt>Physical validation</dt><dd>NOT_ESTABLISHED</dd></div><div><dt>Hardware safety</dt><dd>NOT_ESTABLISHED</dd></div></dl>
    <p><strong>Next engineering action:</strong> establish the real alloy, temperature-dependent properties, allowables, actual tube-sheet restraint, load combinations and relevant failure modes. Then select and qualify the conventional model and compare with independent physical evidence. A larger model or finer mesh cannot supply missing requirements.</p>
    <button type="button" data-hx-ask="Create competing hypotheses about what could make this simple tube model inadequate for a real heat exchanger. Propose the smallest useful next engineering check and identify which physical changes require human approval. Keep hardware safety NOT_ESTABLISHED.">Ask Aero for the next discriminating check ↗</button>
  </section>
  <footer class="hx-controls"><button type="button" data-hx-back>← Previous</button><span data-hx-position>Step 1 of 6</span><button type="button" data-hx-next>Review assumptions →</button></footer>
  <div class="hx-links"><button type="button" data-hx-export>Download evidence JSON</button><a href="/software/aero/first-principles/">Full proof & compiled reference PDF ↗</a></div>
  <p class="hx-muted">Export .tex downloads this evolving notebook. It is source for external compilation, not a live PDF compiler. No GPU, private agent or model connection is required for the calculations.</p>
</section>
<style>
  [data-hx-walkthrough]{color:var(--doc-ink);min-width:0}.hx-heading small,.hx-number{font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--doc-accent)}.hx-heading h3{font-size:21px;line-height:1.25;letter-spacing:-.03em;margin:8px 0}.hx-heading p,p{font-size:12px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--doc-muted)}.hx-scope{font-size:10px;color:var(--doc-accent);border-left:2px solid var(--doc-accent);padding:8px 12px;background:var(--doc-card)}.hx-summary{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:8px;margin:14px 0}.hx-summary>div{padding:12px 9px;border:1px solid var(--doc-rule);border-radius:7px;background:var(--doc-card)}.hx-summary small{display:block;font-size:9px;color:var(--doc-muted)}.hx-summary strong{font-size:15px;display:block;margin-top:7px}.hx-live-note{font-size:10px;min-height:18px;color:var(--doc-warning)}h4{font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;margin:8px 0}.hx-callout{background:var(--doc-card);border:1px solid var(--doc-rule);border-left:3px solid var(--doc-accent);border-radius:7px;padding:12px;font-size:12px;margin:12px 0}.hx-callout p{margin:6px 0 0}.hx-diagram{width:100%;height:auto;color:var(--doc-accent)}.hx-inputs{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px;background:var(--doc-card);border:1px solid var(--doc-rule);padding:14px;border-radius:8px}.hx-inputs label{display:grid;gap:7px;font-size:11px}.hx-inputs input{width:100%;min-width:0;border:1px solid var(--doc-rule);background:var(--doc-input);color:var(--doc-ink);border-radius:5px;padding:9px;font:inherit}.hx-inputs input:invalid{border-color:var(--doc-warning)}button{background:var(--doc-button);color:var(--doc-ink);border:1px solid var(--doc-rule);padding:9px 12px;border-radius:6px;cursor:pointer;font:inherit;font-size:11px}button:disabled{opacity:.5;cursor:default}.hx-table{overflow-x:auto}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:11px;margin:12px 0}th,td{text-align:left;padding:10px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--doc-rule)}th{color:var(--doc-muted);font-weight:500}img{max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:8px}.hx-controls{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:10px;border-top:1px solid var(--doc-rule);padding:16px 0 4px;margin-top:18px}.hx-controls span{color:var(--doc-muted);font-size:10px}.hx-links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;align-items:center;font-size:11px;margin-top:12px}.hx-links a{color:var(--doc-accent);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px}.hx-muted{font-size:10px}.hx-disposition{font-size:11px;display:grid;gap:8px}.hx-disposition>div{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:14px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--doc-rule);padding:9px 0}.hx-disposition dt{color:var(--doc-muted)}.hx-disposition dd{margin:0;text-align:right;color:var(--doc-accent)}:global([data-hx-walkthrough] .proof-equation){--border:var(--doc-rule);--surface:var(--doc-card);--muted:var(--doc-muted);--text:var(--doc-ink);font-size:11px;margin:12px 0}:global(.hx-substitution .katex-display){overflow:auto;padding:6px 0;font-size:.85em}:global(.hx-substitution p){color:var(--doc-muted);font-size:11px}@media(max-width:1000px){.hx-summary{grid-template-columns:1fr}.hx-summary>div{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:8px;align-items:center}.hx-summary strong{margin:0}.hx-heading h3{font-size:18px}}@media(max-width:420px){.hx-inputs{grid-template-columns:1fr}.hx-controls{flex-wrap:wrap}.hx-disposition>div{flex-wrap:wrap}.hx-disposition dd{text-align:left}}
</style>
